e\": \"1.5mm\"}, {\"@type\": \"PropertyValue\", \"name\": \"Brightness\", \"value\": \"1000 nits\"}, {\"@type\": \"PropertyValue\", \"name\": \"Warranty\", \"value\": \"3 Years Standard | 5 Years Extended Available\"}]}10:Tabd,{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What makes the GameWall 240Hz ideal for competitive gaming?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The GameWall 240Hz features a native 240Hz refresh rate and under 3ms input lag, ensuring ultra-smooth visuals and minimal delay. This responsiveness is crucial for high-level competitive gameplay.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What are the available sizes for the GameWall 240Hz?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The GameWall 240Hz comes in three large sizes: 100\\\", 120\\\", and 150\\\", providing an expansive viewing area suitable for immersive gaming experiences and home cinemas.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How does the GameWall handle variable refresh rate (VRR)?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"It supports both AMD FreeSync and NVIDIA G-SYNC VRR technologies, effectively eliminating screen tearing and stuttering for fluid gameplay on compatible gaming PCs and consoles.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What inputs are available on this LED wall?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The GameWall 240Hz is equipped with HDMI 2.1 and DisplayPort 2.0 inputs, supporting up to 4K resolution at 240Hz to meet modern gaming standards.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How is the GameWall 240Hz different from traditional gaming monitors or TVs?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Unlike conventional monitors, the GameWall offers a significantly larger LED canvas with superior brightness (1000 nits) and a pixel pitch of 1.5mm for sharp visuals. Its massive scale and professiona